---
garden: @@GARDEN@@
extends: core@@@VERSION@@
daftar_release: "@@RELEASE@@"  # the daftar release this garden runs; bin/dmupgrade.py moves it
gardener:                      # who keeps this garden: the id of their bean, a person or an organisation
zone: @@ZONE@@                   # the civil time zone this garden reckons its days in: the place half of every day it writes without saying where
---
# @@GARDEN@@

This garden's manifest. It tells a cold agent which garden it is in, whose it is, and which law governs it: the
core, at the version `extends` pins.

A garden is kept by its gardener — a person or an organisation. Write their bean, then name it above in
`gardener:`; the gate asks for it as soon as the garden holds a bean, so it comes first. An agent tends the
garden, and what is not an agent's to decide is the gardener's (manifesto: parts); for an organisation, a person
who answers for it gives that word.

A garden grown to rehearse or to test says so, in a line of its own above: `test: "<what it rehearses>"`.
A rehearsal is grown as a garden of its own, never cloned from a real one: a clone is the same garden.

A garden's identity is the root of its history. Git holds it, so it is written nowhere here:
`python3 bin/propose.py id` prints it.
